  "summary": "Twee pop is a subgenre of indie pop that originally emerged in the United Kingdom during the mid-to late 1980s. The style has been described as \"excessively or affectedly quaint, pretty, or sentimental\" and initially rose to prominence through the NME's C86 cassette compilation, with AllMusic describing twee as \"simplicity and innocence\" as well as \"boy-girl harmonies, lovelorn lyrics, infectious melodies, and simple, unaffected performances\".",
